WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:02.100
(melancholy music)

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.130
I tried running too.

3
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:04.963
It doesn't work.

4
00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:05.796
It always follows.

5
00:00:05.796 --> 00:00:07.970
All due respect, that's your life, not mine.

6
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:08.803
I'm not so sure about that.

7
00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:10.420
What do you want from me lady?

8
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.280
Hey, watch your tone new girl.

9
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.870
You know how they always say it goes back to the original?

10
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.400
Here's the original.

11
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.480
I want your help because you're wrong,

12
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.990
this is your life now, which means that whoever this is,

13
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.410
is gonna keep coming for you.

14
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.720
So?
So I want you

15
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.920
to help us kill him.

16
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.550
You want me to help you

17
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:31.120
and the host of a morning show commit murder?

18
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.221
Correct?
Yeah.

19
00:00:32.221 --> 00:00:34.413
(audience cheer and clap)

20
00:00:34.413 --> 00:00:38.017
Hey, if you can't beat 'em, join 'em!

21
00:00:38.017 --> 00:00:41.960
That's Courtney Cox and Neve Campbell in the new "Scream".

22
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.982
And we are here along with David Arquette.

23
00:00:44.982 --> 00:00:47.481
(audience cheer and clap)

24
00:00:47.481 --> 00:00:50.022
All right, this is what we've got, it's the final thought.

25
00:00:50.022 --> 00:00:53.942
(drum roll)
(audience cheer and clap)

26
00:00:53.942 --> 00:00:56.860
All right, I'm gonna ask each one of you quick,

27
00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.520
rapid fire questions.

28
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.700
David, worst habit during the movie.

29
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.404
Drinking has been the worst habit,

30
00:01:04.404 --> 00:01:06.863
(indistinct) thank goodness.

31
00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:10.480
Neve, what was your worst habit during the movie?

32
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.080
We were staying at the DoubleTree Hotel

33
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.100
and they had cookies on the pillowcase every day,

34
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.228
and I ate those cookies every single day.

35
00:01:17.228 --> 00:01:18.490
(audience laughs)

36
00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.333
Courtney, what was your worst habit during the movie?

37
00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.150
I wonder if I smoked then?

38
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.460
I probably did, yeah.

39
00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:26.430
Did I?
Yeah.

40
00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.260
Smoking cigarettes.

41
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.870
David, what is the scariest thing about you?

42
00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:33.763
Well, I beat myself up.

43
00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:36.900
I'm just very critical of myself

44
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.323
and that's the toughest thing.

45
00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:45.300
Nev what's the scariest thing about you?

46
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.050
I'm Canadian, there's not a whole lot scary about us,

47
00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.070
Yeah, I don't know honestly.

48
00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.800
I'm passing it to you.

49
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.880
I think mine would be my critical voice.

50
00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.253
Maybe not in the same way,

51
00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.880
dealing with, as I get older

52
00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.960
and all the other things you do to criticize yourself

53
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.260
as opposed to just accept.

54
00:02:08.425 --> 00:02:09.920
That would probably be the scariest, the voice.

55
00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.763
David, have you ever seen a ghost in real life?

56
00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.410
I don't know, I feel the energy sometimes,

57
00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:20.810
but I don't think I've seen a ghost in real life.

58
00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:21.643
Neve?

59
00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:23.920
There was a house that I owned,

60
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.610
the very first house I owned that someone passed away in

61
00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:30.550
and I was not the only person to have experiences

62
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:31.790
in that house.

63
00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:34.870
Courtney, have you ever seen a ghost in real life?

64
00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:35.900
I haven't seen a ghost,

65
00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.780
but I did live in a house that was believed to be haunted.

66
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.670
I entered the door one day and there was a UPS guy

67
00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.837
or a FedEx person there, and they said,

68
00:02:46.837 --> 00:02:49.710
"Do you know that your house is haunted?"

69
00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.900
And I go, "Well, I've heard that, but why?"

70
00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.811
He goes, "Because there's someone standing behind you."

71
00:02:53.811 --> 00:02:55.840
(Drew gasps)

72
00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.072
That's a good, scary one.
That's a good one.

73
00:02:58.072 --> 00:02:59.560
That's a really good.
(audience laugh)

74
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.410
Okay, last question.

75
00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.073
How did this movie change you David?

76
00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.710
We had a daughter out of it

77
00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.950
and she's the greatest thing in my life.

78
00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:16.950
And yeah, so that really is the most impactful thing

79
00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:19.620
that's ever happened to me

80
00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.483
in this business.
Yeah.

81
00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.253
Neve, how did this movie change you?

82
00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.240
I mean, this movie gave me everything.

83
00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.900
It was a springboard, I think for all of us.

84
00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.300
I mean, its success really helped pave the way

85
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.060
for all of us in our careers,

86
00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.930
and my life would be very, very different without "Scream".

87
00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.360
Yeah, I hear you on that.

88
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.930
Courtney, how did this movie change you?

89
00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.710
Well, besides the obvious,

90
00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:50.710
I will not go to the bathroom in a movie theater

91
00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.286
or just about any sports arena.

92
00:03:53.286 --> 00:03:54.380
It doesn't matter.

93
00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.790
I always sit underneath and prefer just not to go.

94
00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.670
I will not go into a parking lot by myself.

95
00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.590
And if I do, my heart is racing

96
00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.590
and I'm constantly looking.

97
00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:08.870
Okay, I'm so honored to be a part of this journey

98
00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.020
with you guys.

99
00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.370
And I congratulate you

100
00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.433
with all of my heart
(audience cheer and clap)

101
00:04:13.433 --> 00:04:16.516
for 25 years on "Scream".
Thank you.

102
00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:26.050
Also, everyone in our studio audience is going to go home

103
00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:31.050
with this 4K ultra HD DVD
(audience cheer and clap)

104
00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:34.880
because it's out for the very first time like this.

105
00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.853
Thank you to Paramount Home Entertainment.

106
00:04:37.853 --> 00:04:41.534
(audience cheer and clap)

107
00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:46.534
"Scream" 2022 premiers this Friday, January 14th.

108
00:04:46.657 --> 00:04:48.300
And we'll be right back.

109
00:04:49.294 --> 00:04:54.294
I love you guys.
(upbeat music)

110
00:04:54.446 --> 00:04:57.029 line:15%
(upbeat music)

